// A digit the radix does not admit is the mistake, and is what gets reported.
//
// `0b1012` said "expected `)` to close this call, found `2`", because the
// literal ended silently at the `2` and the parser then complained about
// whatever was left over — which sends the reader looking for a missing
// bracket. `0xfg` did the same with a letter.
//
// Nothing legal can touch the end of a radix literal: an operator or a `.`
// needs no space but is neither a letter nor a digit, and `0b101 and true` has
// a space.
print(0b1012)
